; expect 42
; A `handle` and the operations it handles must resolve their effect by
; the same rule, or they install and read different globals.
;
; Effect operations live in the same table as functions, so they follow
; the module-local rule `850-module-local-binding.ax` pins. The effect a
; `handle` installs is resolved separately. Make one module-local and
; not the other and this program - which is valid, and which both
; compilers accept - exits **71**, the unhandled-effect trap:
; `EffOwn.ownRun` installs its handler in one module's slot while its
; own `log` dispatches on another's. Measured, in exactly that state,
; before the two lookups were paired.
;
; 21 doubled by `EffOwn`'s own handler is 42. The entry file's handler
; returns 99 and must never run: an effect declared in two modules is
; two effects, with two slots, and stage0 has always given them
; separate globals - it was only resolution that conflated them.
(import EffOwn)

(effect Console
  (log :: (-> Int Int)))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (handle (ownRun 21) (Console Alloc) (lambda (v) 99))
)
